From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 23:10:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132-j604: give the SEP its power
 domains

Every deep suspend on the J604 is refused in device suspend:

  apple_sep 3aa600000.sep: sleep refused: irreversible request could
  not be staged (ENOENT)

sep_pm_commit_prepare() reads the enclave's power state through the
first power-domains phandle of the SEP node, so the commit can see the
enclave gate itself. The J604 node has none, and ps_sep was disabled,
so the stage fails with -ENOENT and the PM core falls back to s2idle.

Do as the J713 does: name ps_sep (firmware-owned, never switched by
the kernel) and give the SEP ps_sep and ps_gpio. The J604's own PMGR
map places SEP at +0xc00 and GPIO at +0x120 of the PMGR block, which
are the existing ps_sep and ps_gpio nodes, and its ADT marks the SEP
self-power-gated.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi | 16 +++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi
index 095ef1ccc2..bae1d74ec8 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi
@@ -752,8 +752,22 @@ &ps_avd_sys {
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
+/*
+ * The enclave gates its own domain (ADT: self-power-gate; the J604's
+ * PMGR map has SEP at +0xc00 and GPIO at +0x120). Named, not switched:
+ * the sleep's commit reads its state to see the enclave gate.
+ */
 &ps_sep {
-	status = "disabled";
+	apple,firmware-owned;
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&sep {
+	/*
+	 * Without a domain the driver cannot stage the enclave's sleep
+	 * request for the commit, and every deep suspend is refused.
+	 */
+	power-domains = <&ps_sep>, <&ps_gpio>;
 };
 
 &ps_venc_dma {
-- 
